> \text A Color is a vec3 that means a colour, so everything GLSL does to a vec3 it does to one -- .rgb, mix, clamp, pow. Its window is chosen from the dropdown beside it while the pointer is on it: a picker, the RGB cube, or the HSV cylinder. A marker's fill is its value and its rim says which variable; drag one to choose. Right-drag turns the cube and the cylinder.
end
